WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:15.049
My mom keeps the ice pack in the freezer.

2
00:00:15.050 --> 00:00:20.650
She'd bought it for Tate when he sprained his ankle during basketball practice.

3
00:00:20.651 --> 00:00:24.342
I opened the freezer and got out the ice pack.

4
00:00:24.343 --> 00:00:26.671
Then I put it on top of my head.

5
00:00:26.672 --> 00:00:29.709
It felt really good!

6
00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:36.195
"Don't melt my ice pack with your hot head, Iggy!" said Tate.

7
00:00:36.196 --> 00:00:39.648
"Can I try it?" asked Caswell.

8
00:00:39.649 --> 00:00:46.097
"Quiet, Caswell!" whispered Molly. "Iggy is thinking!"

9
00:00:46.098 --> 00:00:51.321
"Is your brain getting cooler?" asked Jenny hopefully.

10
00:00:51.322 --> 00:00:58.244
"Shh!" said Josh. "Let Iggy think!"

11
00:00:58.245 --> 00:01:01.710
"The ice pack is starting to work," I said after a moment.

12
00:01:01.711 --> 00:01:04.568
"I'm getting an idea."

13
00:01:04.569 --> 00:01:10.415
Josh, Jenny, Molly, and Caswell watched me, waiting to hear my idea.

14
00:01:10.416 --> 00:01:14.184
"It's not exactly an invention," I told them.

15
00:01:14.185 --> 00:01:18.776
"But it is a way for us to stay cool."

16
00:01:18.777 --> 00:01:22.115
I put the ice pack back in the freezer.

17
00:01:22.116 --> 00:01:24.745
Everyone was still looking at me.

18
00:01:24.746 --> 00:01:28.263
"We can go to the movies!" I said.

19
00:01:28.264 --> 00:01:33.373
"The movie theater is air-conditioned, and we will stay nice and cool there."

20
00:01:33.374 --> 00:01:36.108
Josh looked disappointed.

21
00:01:36.109 --> 00:01:39.406
"I don't think my dad will let us go to the movies again.

22
00:01:39.407 --> 00:01:42.403
We just went to see a movie last week."

23
00:01:42.404 --> 00:01:46.428
"Movies cost a lot," said Jenny.

24
00:01:46.429 --> 00:01:51.073
"And the snacks cost even more!" added Molly.

25
00:01:51.074 --> 00:01:52.851
I held up my hand.

26
00:01:52.852 --> 00:01:55.837
"Just a minute," I said.

27
00:01:55.838 --> 00:01:58.682
"I told you only part of my idea.

28
00:01:58.683 --> 00:02:03.065
I thought of a way for us to earn money for the movie too.

29
00:02:03.066 --> 00:02:08.184
We can ask people in our apartment building if they need help doing chores."

30
00:02:08.185 --> 00:02:10.742
Jenny's face brightened.

31
00:02:10.743 --> 00:02:15.938
"Everyone is so hot, they'll be glad to have our help!"

32
00:02:15.939 --> 00:02:23.404
"You'd better ask Mom if it's okay to knock on our neighbors' doors," said Tate.

33
00:02:23.405 --> 00:02:26.859
Just at that moment, my mom came through the door.

34
00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:30.570
She was pulling her shopping cart.

35
00:02:30.571 --> 00:02:35.006
"Whew!" she said. "It's really hot out there!"

36
00:02:35.007 --> 00:02:37.785
She looked at the dark apartment.

37
00:02:37.786 --> 00:02:42.642
"And I guess the power still hasn't come back on."

38
00:02:42.643 --> 00:02:45.185
"Nope," said Josh.

39
00:02:45.186 --> 00:02:50.915
"But Iggy has thought of a way for us to stay cool!"

40
00:02:50.916 --> 00:02:53.906
I told my mom about my idea.

41
00:02:53.907 --> 00:02:59.509
She said it was great, as long as my friends got permission from their parents.

42
00:02:59.510 --> 00:03:03.152
And then she offered to take us to the movies later.

43
00:03:03.153 --> 00:03:07.546
"We can all stay cool together," she said.

44
00:03:07.547 --> 00:03:10.131
"Cool!" said Tate.

45
00:03:10.132 --> 00:03:19.561
We all laughed because Tate always says "cool" when he thinks something is really great.

46
00:03:19.562 --> 00:03:22.261
But this time Tate was right.

47
00:03:22.262 --> 00:03:25.925
Staying cool was cool!

48
00:03:25.926 --> 00:03:30.731
That afternoon we all worked together to earn money to go to the movies.

49
00:03:30.732 --> 00:03:34.720
We swept the front steps for Mr. Calabria.

50
00:03:34.721 --> 00:03:38.669
We took out four bags of junk for Mrs. Carroll.

51
00:03:38.670 --> 00:03:44.687
We took Dr. Stanley's dog for a walk.

52
00:03:44.688 --> 00:03:49.937
We scrubbed the kitchen floor for Molly and Caswell's mom.

53
00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:55.149
Then we sat down on the front steps outside to count our money.

54
00:03:55.150 --> 00:04:01.084
"We have 21 dollars and 45 cents," said Josh.

55
00:04:01.085 --> 00:04:07.565
"That's only enough for two of us to go to the movies!" Molly said, disappointed.

56
00:04:07.566 --> 00:04:13.161
"And only enough to buy half a bag of popcorn," I added.

57
00:04:13.162 --> 00:04:18.438
"We could flip a coin to decide who can go to the movies," said Josh.

58
00:04:18.439 --> 00:04:24.425
"That's no fun," said Jenny. "We all worked hard today."

59
00:04:24.426 --> 00:04:26.322
Molly looked at me.

60
00:04:26.323 --> 00:04:32.179
"Maybe Iggy can think of how we can all go to the movies," she said.

61
00:04:32.180 --> 00:04:37.814
"Iggy had better put on his ice pack again," said Caswell.

62
00:04:37.815 --> 00:04:44.362
I nodded. Sweat was streaming down my face.

63
00:04:44.363 --> 00:04:49.555
We went upstairs to get the ice pack out of the freezer.

64
00:04:49.556 --> 00:04:53.447
But do you know what we found when we got to my apartment?

65
00:04:53.448 --> 00:05:00.783
The ice pack was melting!
